/*
A real block comment that mentions the import form must not be scanned as one.

The dependency scanner walked every line looking for a line that is exactly
`import (` and then took the first quoted string on the lines that followed,
with no notion of comments. Inside a line comment that cannot happen, because
every line begins with `//`. Inside a real block comment it can, and the scanner
then adds a package that exists only in prose to the import list:

import (
	"example.com/not/a/real/package"
)

The prose block's closing line is `*/` rather than `)`, so the block scan also
kept consuming the rest of the file looking for a line that is exactly `)`.
extractImports now delegates to scanFileRegions, which classifies each line's
CODE and tracks block-comment state, so one comment-aware scanner replaces two
that could drift.
*/
package main

import (
	"time"
)

func main() {
	// Termination: a batch program must still be stoppable, so the entry
	// handles the channel the runtime closes on SIGINT/SIGTERM.
	select {
	case <-sigint:
		return
	default:
	}

	if time.UTC() == nil {
		panic("no UTC")
	}
}
